/target

# Secrets and local credentials. The !.env.example line keeps the committed
# sample visible (github/gitignore Node.gitignore uses exactly this triple).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Claude Code working files. A global git ignore file may block these too, but
# that is per-machine and invisible to clones, so the rule lives here.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
